---
// Terms of Use, Acceptable Use, and Privacy — combined into one page.
// Public + indexable.
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="color-scheme" content="light dark" />
    <title>Terms, Privacy &amp; Acceptable Use — Brambletally</title>
    <meta name="description" content="Terms of Use, Acceptable Use, and Privacy for Brambletally." />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <link rel="preload" href="/fonts/eb-garamond-400-latin.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin />
    <style>
      @font-face { font-family:'Alegreya Sans'; font-weight:400; font-display:swap; src:url('/fonts/alegreya-sans-400-latin.woff2') format('woff2'); }
      @font-face { font-family:'Alegreya Sans'; font-weight:700; font-display:swap; src:url('/fonts/alegreya-sans-700-latin.woff2') format('woff2'); }
      @font-face { font-family:'EB Garamond'; font-weight:400; font-display:swap; src:url('/fonts/eb-garamond-400-latin.woff2') format('woff2'); }
      @font-face { font-family:'EB Garamond'; font-weight:600; font-display:swap; src:url('/fonts/eb-garamond-600-latin.woff2') format('woff2'); }
      :root {
        --bg:#f3ecdc; --card:#fbf6ea; --border:#e0d4b8; --border-strong:#a89670;
        --text:#2a2230; --text-sub:#4a3f4e; --text-muted:#6f6374; --accent:#6b3457;
        --head:'EB Garamond',Georgia,serif; --body:'Alegreya Sans',system-ui,sans-serif;
      }
      @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
        :root { --bg:#1e1a22; --card:#292330; --border:#3d3545; --border-strong:#625770;
          --text:#ece3d6; --text-sub:#c7bcae; --text-muted:#948a83; --accent:#c17ba3; }
      }
      * { box-sizing:border-box; }
      body { margin:0; background:var(--bg); color:var(--text); font-family:var(--body);
        font-size:1.0625rem; line-height:1.65; -webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased; }
      .wrap { max-width:64ch; margin:0 auto; padding:32px 24px 72px; }
      a { color:var(--accent); }
      .back { font-size:.9rem; text-decoration:none; color:var(--text-sub); }
      h1 { font-family:var(--head); font-weight:600; font-size:2.2rem; margin:1.5rem 0 .25rem; }
      h2 { font-family:var(--head); font-weight:600; font-size:1.35rem; margin:2rem 0 .5rem;
        scroll-margin-top:1.5rem; }
      h2.section { border-top:1px solid var(--border); padding-top:2rem; margin-top:3rem; }
      p, li { color:var(--text-sub); }
      .meta { color:var(--text-muted); font-size:.9rem; margin-bottom:1.5rem; }
      .jump { list-style:none; margin:0 0 2rem; padding:14px 16px; background:var(--card);
        border:1px solid var(--border); border-radius:10px; display:flex; gap:.5rem 1.25rem; flex-wrap:wrap; }
      .jump a { font-size:.95rem; text-decoration:none; font-weight:600; }
      :focus-visible { outline:2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset:3px; }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <div class="wrap">
      <a class="back" href="/">&larr; Brambletally</a>
      <h1>Terms, Privacy &amp; Acceptable Use</h1>
      <p class="meta">Last updated September 13, 2026</p>

      <ul class="jump">
        <li><a href="#terms">Terms of Use</a></li>
        <li><a href="#acceptable-use">Acceptable Use</a></li>
        <li><a href="#privacy">Privacy</a></li>
        <li><a href="/legal/cookies">Cookies</a></li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="section" id="terms">Terms of Use</h2>

      <h2>Using Brambletally</h2>
      <p>Brambletally is a project tracker for makers. You must be at least 13
      years old to use it. You can use it for your own craft, research, and
      event work, and for projects you share with other signed-in people.</p>

      <h2>Your account</h2>
      <p>Sign-in is a one-time link sent to your email address. Keep access to
      that inbox secure — you're responsible for what happens under your
      account. Tell <a href="mailto:support@brambletally.com">support@brambletally.com</a>
      if you think someone else has access to it.</p>

      <h2>Your content</h2>
      <p>Your projects, steps, supplies, notes, and journal entries are yours.
      Brambletally stores them to run the service and doesn't claim ownership.
      By adding content, you give Brambletally permission to store, back up,
      and show it to you and anyone you share a project with — nothing more.
      People you invite to a project can see it, and editors can change it.</p>

      <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>Follow the <a href="#acceptable-use">Acceptable Use</a> rules below. We
      may remove content or suspend an account that breaks them.</p>

      <h2>Service availability</h2>
      <p>Brambletally is provided as-is and as-available, with no warranty
      that it will be uninterrupted, error-free, or that data will never be
      lost. Features may be added, changed, or removed at any time.</p>

      <h2>Liability</h2>
      <p>To the extent the law allows, Brambletally isn't liable for indirect,
      incidental, or consequential damages arising from your use of the
      service. Its total liability to you for any claim is limited to the
      amount you've paid in the past 12 months.</p>

      <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
      <p>These terms may be updated as Brambletally changes. Material changes
      will be shown at sign-in.</p>

      <h2>Ending your account</h2>
      <p>You can export your data and delete your account from settings at any
      time. Deleting your account removes your personal projects; shared
      projects owned by others are unaffected. An account that violates these
      terms or the Acceptable Use policy may be suspended or closed.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions go to <a href="mailto:support@brambletally.com">support@brambletally.com</a>.</p>

      <h2 class="section" id="acceptable-use">Acceptable Use</h2>
      <p>Brambletally is a small, signed-in space. These rules keep it usable.</p>
      <h2>Don't</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Harass, threaten, or abuse other people.</li>
        <li>Post spam, or content you have no right to share.</li>
        <li>Upload anything illegal or infringing.</li>
        <li>Try to break, overload, or probe the service.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>On shared projects</h2>
      <p>The person who owns a project decides who has access and what stays in
      it. Their call on their own project stands.</p>
      <h2>Enforcement</h2>
      <p>An administrator may remove content or suspend an account that breaks
      these rules. Tell <a href="mailto:support@brambletally.com">support@brambletally.com</a>
      if you run into abuse. When the shared project board ships, it will have
      its own report control and the same rules will apply there.</p>

      <h2 class="section" id="privacy">Privacy</h2>

      <h2>What Brambletally collects</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Your email address, used to sign you in and to reach you about your account.</li>
        <li>The projects, steps, supplies, notes, journal entries, and categories you create.</li>
        <li>A session cookie so you stay signed in (see <a href="/legal/cookies">Cookies</a>).</li>
        <li>Basic technical logs needed to run and secure the service.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Third parties</h2>
      <p>Sign-in links are sent through Resend. Cloudflare Turnstile checks
      that you're not a bot at sign-in, and Cloudflare's network runs the
      service itself. Each processes only the data it needs to do that job —
      none of them see your projects.</p>

      <h2>Sharing</h2>
      <p>Nothing is sold or handed to advertisers. People you invite to a
      project can see its contents. That is the only sharing that happens.</p>

      <h2>Security</h2>
      <p>Brambletally uses standard security practices, including encryption
      in transit, to protect your data. No system is perfectly secure, but
      keeping your data safe is a priority.</p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>Brambletally isn't intended for children under 13, and it doesn't
      knowingly collect information from anyone under that age.</p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>You can export everything tied to your account, and delete your
      account, from settings. Deletion is permanent — your data is removed
      shortly after, except where the law requires it to be kept longer.</p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>Material changes to this policy will be shown at sign-in, the same
      way as changes to the Terms.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Data questions go to <a href="mailto:support@brambletally.com">support@brambletally.com</a>.</p>

      <p style="margin-top:2.5rem"><a class="back" href="/">&larr; Back to Brambletally</a></p>
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
